post.\n2. **N: f6-g4**: This also saves the Knight and attacks f2/h2. However, e4 feels more controlling of the center and restricts White's pieces more effectively.\n3. **B: e6-h3**: This captures the White Knight but likely leads to a trade (Bxh3, then White recaptures or Pxf6). It complicates the game unnecessarily when a simple retreat preserves the material lead.\n4. **Q: h1-e4**: This moves the Queen to the center but allows White to capture the Knight on f6 (Pxf6), losing a piece.\n\nReason: The move N: f6-e4 is the best choice because it saves the Knight from capture, places it on a very active and safe central square, and maintains Black's overwhelming material advantage. It avoids any tactical complications and prepares for a final attack on the White King.\n\nAnswer: N: f6-e4"}
